# --- Developer-only docs (private build planning; not published) ---
# docs/* (not bare `docs`) so the two negations below can re-include the
# execution loop's state anchors; everything else in docs/ stays ignored.
docs/*
!docs/CHANGELOG.log
!docs/evidence/
docs/PRD.md
docs/BUILD_STATUS.md
docs/OPERATING_SCHEDULE.md
docs/old-ref-prompt.md/
spec
python/tests

# NOTE: Cargo.lock IS tracked on purpose.
# This workspace produces binaries (aria-cli, aria-wasm cdylib), so per
# Cargo convention the lockfile is committed for reproducible builds.
# https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/faq.html#why-do-binaries-have-cargo-lock-in-version-control-but-not-libraries